<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Taifa of Beja and Évora</h1><p class="st-meta">1144 CE – 1150 CE (approx.) · capital Beja</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived state of the Banu Wazir in the Alentejo, one of the regimes that rose on the ruins of Almoravid power in the 1140s.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1144 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sidray-ibn-wazir">Sidray ibn Wazir</a>, a commander of a local family, took Beja and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/evora">Évora</a> in the revolt against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a>. At first an ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-qasi">Ibn Qasi</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/second-taifa-of-mertola">Second Taifa of Mértola</a>, he soon broke with him, while his relatives held the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/second-taifa-of-badajoz">Second Taifa of Badajoz</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The territory covered the wheat lands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alentejo">Alentejo</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tagus">Tagus</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algarve">Algarve</a>, a frontier exposed to raids from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-portugal">Kingdom of Portugal</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sidray-ibn-wazir">Sidray</a> ruled as a military strongman and became one of the leading figures of the western revolt.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 1150 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sidray-ibn-wazir">Sidray</a> submitted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a>, who kept him as a governor. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/evora">Évora</a> was captured for Portugal in 1165 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gerald-the-fearless">Gerald the Fearless</a>, and Beja was taken definitively in 1234.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1144 CE – 1150 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:82.47%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1144 CE – 1150 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Beja</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sidray ibn Wazir</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Andalusi Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/portugal">Portugal</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Taifa of Évora</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1147&amp;focus=taifa-of-beja-and-evora" aria-label="Taifa of Beja and Évora on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4484 811 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Taifa of Beja and Évora lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4804 1067L4799 1289M4804 1067L4794 1282"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4799 1289h0M4794 1282h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4804 1067h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4804 1067h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Beja. <a href="/atlas?year=1147&amp;focus=taifa-of-beja-and-evora">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
